   "entry": "2026-10-12 HAND-BACK slice 83, scenario \"Two creates carrying the same key leave the shop untouched\" | test tests/test_make_several_changes_at_once.py::test_two_creates_carrying_the_same_key_leave_the_shop_untouched: an existing test can only stay green by being rewritten, and the task does not list it under Tests the decisions break. kb.v2 has no batch key (CreateItem.key reserved), so no kb refusal names a key; D3 says only that a @key resolves to the IRI the seam gives that create, and nothing what a key two creates carry is. With no link written to the shared key, the batch lands. Evidence: tests/test_make_several_changes_at_once.py:163 assert faults and any(fault.rule == LINK and key in printed(fault) for fault in faults) fails: kb's answer to the same BatchCreate, asked after shop-knol's, is two faults rule 'identity', 'an IRI names one artifact; the store already holds one at ...', since shop-knol's apply had landed both creates. Decision needed: who refuses a key two creates carry under kb.v2 (shop-knol in its own words, which the Then's kb-words oracle does not allow), and what the Then becomes. Green in this slice: 201 of 202 (the rest of the suite under kb 0.9.0). Red: that scenario."
  }
